From 0c536c4d879d4fdab5635063b8de96bd84e03c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:27:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/57] hw/display: SSD1351 OLED driver and OLED C Click;
 PpPanel for headless views

- pp_panel: what a display panel shows, for front ends without a QEMU
  console: "frame" (base64 RGB565), "frame-gen" (bumped on change),
  "panel-width"/"panel-height", composed on demand by the controller's
  render callback. Meant for every SPI/parallel display controller
  (ST7789 next).
- ssd1351: SSD1351 data sheet rev 1.3, 4-wire SPI: column/row windows,
  Write RAM (65k and 262k), re-map and colour swap, start line, offset,
  MUX ratio, display modes, sleep, the command lock and the commands it
  protects after reset; other commands take their parameters and are
  ignored; scrolling not modelled. D/C, RES# and the panel's supply are
  GPIO inputs. Panel geometry properties; the defaults are the OLED C
  Click's PSP27801 (96x96 on SEG111..16, COM127..32), inferred from
  MikroElektronika's oledc driver.
- mikrobus: OLED C Click "oledc" (schematic v102): CS, D/C on PWM, RES#
  on RST, the 15 V EN on INT; pulls R7 100k (CS), R8 10k (RST), R9 10k
  (EN, down).
- qtests: the mikroSDK init sequence and pixels, BGR order, inverse/all
  on, lock, sleep, supply off, RES#, locked A2h; on mikroBUS 2 of the
  Nano Base too.

Not checked against a physical OLED C Click.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
